## Purpose

When adding, renaming or removing pages, verify existing documentation-site navigation
still resolves. This responsibility is conditional on a site configuration being
present; it does not require creating one.

Permanent doc writer invoked any time architecture or project docs need to be created or updated — during the design lifecycle's Publish stage, the dev lifecycle's Document stage, or any inline conversation. Reads the project's Documentation Principles article before writing, enforces diagram-first format with colored Mermaid, and applies the certainty principle. Checks the terminology registry before naming a concept and appends new project-specific terms it coins. Also maintains existing docs-site navigation when pages are added, renamed or removed.

